      "problem": "Expand $(p^2-q^2)(2p+3q).$",
      "worked_solution": "We take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({p}^{2}-{q}^{2})(2p+3q) & = \\\\ {p}^{2}(2p+3q)+(-{q}^{2})(2p+3q) & = \\\\ 2{p}^{3}+3{p}^{2}q-2p{q}^{2}-3{q}^{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot simplify the above expression any further because there are no like terms.",
